<h1>Script Generation</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>In therms of KUBE a file containing sequence of macro commands is named script. A macro command could be either recorded during execution of various functions in KUBE or manually written by the user.</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Automatic script generation</b></span> - used for quick recording script commands. Procedure:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">Open a file</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">Call the functions necessary for processing the file.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">When data processing is complete, save the file and close it</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">Press F11 and the <a href="Macros_Menu/show_command_window.htm">log window</a> will appear. As you see it contains record of all executed functions for the current KUBE session.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">Select the sequence of commands, that you want to save as script, and copy it in the clipboard.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">Paste the clipboard content in a text editor and save it as .txt file. This file (without making any other changes) can be used later as script and executed for a single file only.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Manual script generation</b></span>. Procedure:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">If you know very well the KUBE script commands you could write manually the whole command sequence in a txt file and use it later as script. The process is slower than the automatic generation and mistakes can be easily made.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">Scripts written manually can be very flexible and executed on multiple files, but the user should be careful and keep the writing rules and conventions.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mixed script generation</b></span> - recommended as quick and flexible enough. Procedure:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">Generate a script using the automatic procedure.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">Open the saved script file and make changes manually: for example add functions, include predefined or custom parameters, remove useless commands, add comments, etc.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered">
<p class="Numbered">Save the script file - it is ready for use now on single as well as on multiple files.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="ExampleCode">2 Examples for mixed script generation:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Initial automatic script generation:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Open( FileName="D:\temp\CAD.sab2" )<br>
OpenInDoc( FileName="D:\temp\scan1.sab2" )<br>
SaveAs( FileName="D:\Temp\aligned1.sab2" )<br>
CloseFile( FileName="D:\Temp\aligned1.sab2" )</p>
<p id="P1" class="whs4">Comment: If the initial script is executed it will:</p>
<ul type="circle" class="whs5">
<li class="kadov-p-IP1">
<p id="P1" class="whs4">open <span style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif;">CAD.sab2,</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-IP1">
<p id="P1" class="whs6">open scan1.sab2 in the current file,</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-IP1">
<p id="P1" class="whs6">save the file under new name</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-IP1">
<p id="P1" class="whs4"><span style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif;">and finally close it.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="ExampleCode">The script when the manual editing is completed:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode"><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; text-decoration:none;">Open( FileName="D:\temp\CAD.sab2" )<br>
OpenInDoc( FileName=%FileName% )<br>
SelEntityType( Type="PtStripe")<br>
AlignEntities( SmpStep=1, MaxDist=3, IterNum=5, Ref="CAD Model", TrOnly=Yes )<br>
SaveAs( FileName=%FilePath%Aligned_%ShortFileName% )<br>
CloseFile( FileName=%FilePath%Aligned_%ShortFileName% )</span></p>
<p class="whs4">Comment: If the new script is executed it will:</p>
<ul type="circle" class="whs5">
<li class="kadov-p">
<p class="whs4">open the CAD.sab2 file</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p">
<p class="whs4">open in it the currently processed file of the multiple file list</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p">
<p class="whs4">select all scan data entities</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p">
<p class="whs4">align the selection to the <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">CAD Model (</span><span style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif;">this is the content of the</span> CAD.sab2 file)</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p">
<p class="whs4">save the new file in the same folder as the currently processed file, but with name "Aligned_currently processed file name")</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p">
<p class="whs4">close the file</p>
</li>
</ul>
